 "notes": "HIP 75056 Ab was discovered with VLT/SPHERE (IRDIS K1K2 + IFS YJH) as part of the Scorpion Planet Survey (Wagner+2020); the ~12 Myr old A2V primary lies in Upper Centaurus-Lupus (Sco-Cen). Mass ~20-30 Mjup, consistent with the low-mass end of disk-instability formation. Hierarchical triple with a wide (~650 au) low-mass stellar companion HIP 75056 B.",
 "last_updated": "2026-07-06"
